  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0003_5e751872496a.png\"/> </p><p>As the two rods are in series, the force at the connecting surface will be same.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> is Young's modulus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is increase in length, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are lengths, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are areas, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are radii of thick and thin wires respectively.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mtext>∵ F</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>Y</mtext><mo>×</mo><mtext>strain</mtext><mo>×</mo><mtext>Area</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>  </mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
